## The Big Picture

You have two machines fully managed by Nix, with config backed up on GitHub.

```
GitHub (Trizzy71/nix-config)
│
├── MacBook Air (aarch64-darwin)
│   └── home-manager standalone + flakes
│       managed by: home-manager switch
│
└── Dell Latitude 5490 (x86_64-linux)
    └── NixOS + home-manager as NixOS module + flakes
        managed by: nixos-rebuild switch
```

**The core idea:** Your entire system is described in text files. If a machine dies,
you clone your repo, run one command, and your environment is identical to before.
Nothing is manual. Nothing is forgotten.

