## Current Architecture

```
GitHub: Trizzy71/nix-config
├── flake.nix              ← mac entry point
├── flake.lock             ← exact pinned versions (never edit manually)
├── home.nix               ← mac user config
├── linux-home.nix         ← dell user config
├── dell-flake.nix         ← dell system entry point (reference copy)
└── dell-configuration.nix ← dell system config (reference copy)

MacBook: ~/.config/home-manager/
├── flake.nix              ← pins nixpkgs + home-manager from GitHub
├── flake.lock             ← locked versions
└── home.nix               ← your user config (cloned from GitHub)

Dell: /etc/nixos/
├── flake.nix              ← wires NixOS + home-manager together
├── flake.lock             ← locked versions
├── hardware-configuration.nix  ← auto-generated, NEVER touch
├── configuration.nix      ← system level config
└── home.nix               ← copied from linux-home.nix on GitHub
```

### What Each Layer Manages

| Layer | File | Manages |
|---|---|---|
| NixOS system (Dell only) | `configuration.nix` | bootloader, networking, sound, qtile, user accounts, zsh system-wide |
| Dell user config | `home.nix` (from `linux-home.nix`) | neovim, bat, zsh, git, packages, aliases |
| Mac user config | `home.nix` | same as above but macOS paths |

### The One Difference Between Mac and Dell `home.nix`

```nix
# Mac
home.homeDirectory = "/Users/tristan";

# Dell
home.homeDirectory = "/home/tristan";
```

Everything else is identical.

