## Daily Workflow

### Making a Change on the MacBook

```bash
# 1. edit your config
nano ~/.config/home-manager/home.nix

# 2. apply it
hms

# 3. if it works, push to GitHub
cd ~/.config/home-manager
git add .
git commit -m "what you changed"
git push
```

### Making a Change on the Dell

```bash
# 1. edit config(s)
sudo nano /etc/nixos/home.nix
sudo nano /etc/nixos/configuration.nix  # only if changing system stuff

# 2. dry run first
sudo nixos-rebuild dry-run --flake /etc/nixos#nixos-test

# 3. apply
sudo nixos-rebuild switch --flake /etc/nixos#nixos-test

# 4. push to GitHub
cd ~/nix-config
cp /etc/nixos/home.nix linux-home.nix
git add .
git commit -m "what you changed"
git push
```

### Pulling Mac Changes onto the Dell

```bash
cd ~/nix-config
git pull
sudo cp ~/nix-config/linux-home.nix /etc/nixos/home.nix
sudo nixos-rebuild switch --flake /etc/nixos#nixos-test
```

### Pulling Dell Changes onto the Mac

```bash
cd ~/.config/home-manager
git pull
hms
```

