## Growth Areas

These are natural next steps when you're ready, roughly in order:

### Near Term
- **Customize neovim further** — add plugins like `nvim-treesitter` (better syntax
  highlighting), `telescope.nvim` (fuzzy file finding), `nvim-lspconfig` (IDE features)
- **Add starship prompt** — a fast, beautiful shell prompt. `programs.starship.enable = true;`
- **Explore bat themes** — run `bat --list-themes` to preview all available themes
- **Add more shell aliases** — make your workflow faster

### Medium Term
- **Make `/etc/nixos` a git repo** — eliminates the manual copy step when updating
  the Dell, everything stays in sync automatically
- **Split `common.nix`** — put shared config in one file, Mac/Linux differences
  in separate files. Cleaner and easier to maintain across machines
- **Manage qtile config via home-manager** — your window manager config becomes
  declarative and version controlled like everything else

### Longer Term
- **Unified root flake** — one `flake.nix` at the root of your repo that defines
  all machines. Build any machine's config from any other machine
- **Add tailscale nodes** — new `nixosConfigurations` entries for server nodes,
  managed from the same repo
- **nix-darwin** — if you want to manage macOS system-level settings declaratively
  (dock, keyboard, system preferences) the same way NixOS manages Linux
- **Deploy-rs or colmena** — tools for deploying NixOS configs to remote machines
  over SSH, useful once you have multiple servers

### Useful Resources
- https://search.nixos.org/packages — search all available packages
- https://search.nixos.org/options — search all NixOS options
- https://home-manager-options.extradoc.io — search all home-manager options
- https://nixos.wiki — community wiki with guides and examples
- https://nix.dev — official learning resource
- https://nixos.org/manual/nixpkgs/stable — nixpkgs manual

